From: Christian Andrej Görlach <cgoerlac@gmail.com>
Subject: [SRU][N][PATCH 1/1] UBUNTU: SAUCE: io_uring/kbuf: fix inverted reserved-field checks

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2162843

The Noble adaptation of "io_uring/kbuf: use mem_is_zero()" substitutes
memchr_inv() for mem_is_zero() without adjusting the negation. These
helpers have opposite truth values for an all-zero area.

As a result, valid provided-buffer-ring registration, unregistration
and status requests fail with EINVAL, while nonzero reserved bytes
are accepted by these checks.

Remove the three negations to reject nonzero reserved bytes and accept
valid zero-filled requests. This restores the original validation
semantics without changing allocation or ring lifetime handling.

Signed-off-by: Christian Andrej Görlach <cgoerlac@gmail.com>
---
 io_uring/kbuf.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/io_uring/kbuf.c b/io_uring/kbuf.c
--- a/io_uring/kbuf.c
+++ b/io_uring/kbuf.c
@@ -549,7 +549,7 @@
 
 	if (copy_from_user(&reg, arg, sizeof(reg)))
 		return -EFAULT;
-	if (!memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)))
+	if (memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 	if (reg.flags & ~IOU_PBUF_RING_MMAP)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -608,7 +608,7 @@
 
 	if (copy_from_user(&reg, arg, sizeof(reg)))
 		return -EFAULT;
-	if (!memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)) || reg.flags)
+	if (memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)) || reg.flags)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	bl = io_buffer_get_list(ctx, reg.bgid);
@@ -629,7 +629,7 @@
 
 	if (copy_from_user(&buf_status, arg, sizeof(buf_status)))
 		return -EFAULT;
-	if (!memchr_inv(buf_status.resv, 0, sizeof(buf_status.resv)))
+	if (memchr_inv(buf_status.resv, 0, sizeof(buf_status.resv)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	bl = io_buffer_get_list(ctx, buf_status.buf_group);
